Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.30,Cap,And so if you were to buy a property for,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.30,0:00:05.40,Cap,call it 400K, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.40,0:00:08.10,Cap,And then you were to sell that property
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.10,0:00:09.70,Cap,two years later or a year later,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.70,0:00:12.30,Cap,let's say for 430K,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.30,0:00:14.20,Cap,you actually lost a little bit of money
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.20,0:00:15.30,Cap,when you think about it, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.30,0:00:17.50,Cap,If you're at that 10%, you bought it for 400K,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.50,0:00:21.00,Cap,you sold it for 430, you just lost about 43.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:26.10,Cap,So you actually came out net 393, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.10,0:00:28.60,Cap,So net, you lost 7K when you factor in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.60,0:00:30.90,Cap,some of the closing costs and things of that nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.90,0:00:33.80,Cap,And so it behooves you to hold onto a property
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.80,0:00:35.10,Cap,minimum five years.
